BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (Action: Turn on busy-signal rerouting, a short ring timeout and duplicate routing for repeat callers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (Detail: Ringba checks in milliseconds whether the person has called before and routes them to buyer two,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (which has no relationship with that caller and treats it as fresh [Ringba - ojcbZuG798w @ 00:16:51].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 556.75 Tm (Mattias Mesters walks through the core routing plan math in Ringba: priority one targets are always tried) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.52 Tm (first, priority two only when none of them is available, and within a tier the weights become fractions, so) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (targets weighted 1, 6, 6 and 1 split traffic 1/14, 6/14, 6/14 and 1/14 [0eCCbtHmCJE @ 00:02:34]. Error) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (handling sits on top. Adam describes Ringba detecting a busy signal within a few milliseconds and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (immediately dialing buyer two, fast enough that no caller can notice, which neutralizes call centers that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (oversell capacity to many publishers and then busy-signal overflow so they never pay for it [ojcbZuG798w @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm (00:05:07]. For buyers who let calls ring 30 seconds instead of bouncing them, the fix is a ring timeout) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm (configured at the buyer or target level, maybe five seconds, maybe ten, after which the call is pulled and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm (rerouted [ojcbZuG798w @ 00:08:15]. Adam pairs that with a commercial term: if a ringing buyer imposes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (duration requirements, bill on duration from the moment the call starts ringing rather than from answer,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (because the buyer captured the option value of picking up the whole time [ojcbZuG798w @ 00:06:38]. Adam) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.27 Tm (actually prefers busy-signal buyers, since the bounce arrives in real time.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.05 Tm (Simultaneous dialing rings every eligible buyer at once, whether three or 600, and the first to answer wins) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.82 Tm (the call, but Adam flags the trap: if buyer one pays $10, buyer two $22 and buyer three $6, and buyer three) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.60 Tm (always answers fastest, sim-dial gets expensive, and mixed West Coast and East Coast requirements break) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 328.37 Tm (it too [ojcbZuG798w @ 00:11:41]. The ideal setup is nationwide buyers paying roughly the same, such as) Tj ET
