0.6 w 54.00 747.00 m 558.00 747.00 l S
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (Every operator who addresses the rule lands on the same core shift. Consent now attaches to one named) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (business, and the 'our partners' blanket is finished. Evocalize sets the bar as a box the consumer physically) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (checks that names the exact downstream contact \(loan officer, agent or provider\), presented 'clear and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (conspicuous.' Evocalize adds that the caller must 'take physical possession of the consent record before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (making the outbound call' [h8PlsMHs16k @ 00:01:27]. Mike Fitzpatrick describes a mandatory per-company) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (checkbox plus a contact-method box. He says the '72 other companies' style of batch consent that powered) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (the old lead-gen loophole is out [N9n3qM6ZlfI @ 00:13:04]. ActiveProspect's Benjamin Nafarro confirms) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (link-out partner lists are no longer allowed. Exclusive sellers now dynamically insert a single company, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (shared sellers move to individual checkboxes that bring more post-rejects [uXTg2yB_ZTM @ 00:14:07].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (StreetText's Jonathan gives the street version: the recipient must see the business receiving consent, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (handing that consent to a second or third business is no longer legal. In his telling, the change ends) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (consumers being 'round robin' by businesses chasing the same lead, which is exactly the reseller loophole) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (the rule targets [5wE-LfVEhgk @ 00:02:09]. For anyone running ping-post or aged-lead resale, the shared) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (conclusion is blunt: the old multi-buyer consent asset no longer carries forward.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (The baseline form mechanics are just as uniform across speakers. TechMarketer's build uses a single select) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (for each item, 'no select all,' and 'no pre-check,' which he calls 'a big one.' Interest is tied to a specific) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (product, the partner-communications option is removable, and a final confirmation step closes the flow) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm ([B9lfPgUUls0 @ 00:00:43]. Pitchit says consent requires affirmative action through an unchecked box and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (cannot be implied from inactivity or browsing. Its framing: 'you can't just assume anything it needs to be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm (Express written consent for very specific use cases' [k6g6hxICGH4 @ 00:04:03]. Seasalt AI's Amy Chan) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (says each regulated technology must be named explicitly in the consent language: automated SMS,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm (recorded voice, IVR, voice drop and AI voice calls. She also rules out pre-checked boxes and consent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (hidden behind a privacy hyperlink [KBFaRW7QmVQ @ 00:18:57]. TrackDrive reduces the record standard) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.82 Tm (to one line operators repeat on every vertical: 'If you can't show who agreed, when, and to what, assume) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.60 Tm (you can't prove it.' It pairs that with a warning that 'vague wording like our partners can be a real problem' for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 335.37 Tm (outbound follow-up [sFVqp8Vluy8 @ 00:03:34]. The working standard that emerges is a named business,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 320.15 Tm (an unchecked box, every channel spelled out, and a record that captures who, when and what.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 304.92 Tm (Practitioners also agree on who carries the risk, and it is the buyer. Pitchit says the buyer bears the burden) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 289.70 Tm (of verifying prior express written consent and must document when, how and where it was obtained. Pitchit) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 274.47 Tm (tells buyers to request the full consent paragraph for their legal team and to add contractual indemnification) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 259.25 Tm ([k6g6hxICGH4 @ 00:00:35]. Eric Troutman says lead sellers create the risk but buyers bear it, with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 244.02 Tm (indemnity flowing back up the chain. He puts it plainly: 'remember if you're a lead buyer the risk is on you') Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 228.80 Tm ([KBFaRW7QmVQ @ 00:33:39]. Fitzpatrick agrees the buyer still bears the burden of proof, and he predicts) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 213.57 Tm (lead cost will 'extremely increase' as the batch-consent supply dries up [N9n3qM6ZlfI @ 00:18:12]. Socius's) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 198.35 Tm (Brian brought the home-service vertical to Socius in 2008 and works with over half the top 500 remodelers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 183.12 Tm (He expects higher cost per lead from aggregators but better quality. In his view, big brands gain while small) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 167.90 Tm (and mid-sized companies are disadvantaged, and bulk-list buyers face the heaviest disruption) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 152.67 Tm ([2YZuiPP4QWc @ 00:08:13]. The consensus economics are pricier, cleaner inventory, with the buyer's own) Tj ET
