BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (to 2 weeks for delivery and send about 10 calls in week one [Ringba - RhODbxB4ylU @ 00:29:34].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 602.42 Tm (Network entry is a numbers game. Ryan Moran's sourcing stack starts with the major newbie-friendly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 587.20 Tm (networks. He adds Offer Vault's pay-per-call filter, Google phrase searches like '[vertical] affiliate network,') Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 571.97 Tm (partner links in site headers and footers, '[company] site:linkedin.com' searches to reach affiliate managers,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 556.75 Tm (and Facebook groups. His numbers: apply to 8 to 12 networks and expect 4 to 6 acceptances) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.52 Tm ([NC4s18S7p00 @ 00:04:32]. Because reviews 'can take weeks,' Moran calls the network right after applying) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (and asks lingo-heavy questions to 'feign competence' [NC4s18S7p00 @ 00:05:31]. Matt Wacek counts) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (roughly 290 pay-per-call offers among about 61,000 on Offervault and says getting accepted matters more) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (than niche. He vets networks on payout frequency, a reply within one business day, and payout thresholds) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (that may sit at $1,000 [pgr3PBjow6g @ 00:05:09]. Wacek pushes emergency niches: fire, smoke, or water) Tj ET
